---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const team = [
    {name: "Spencer Barrett", role: "Frontend: Sign Up Page" },
    { name: "Vineet Gupta", role: "Backend (FastAPI)" },
    { name: "Nick Garza", role: "Frontend: Blog Page" },
    { name: "Mikai Miranda", role: "Frontend: About page" },
];
---

<Layout>
    <main class="hero">
        <div class="overlay"></div>
        <div class="content gap-6">
            <h1>About <span>BiteSwipe</span></h1>

            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                BiteSwipe is a software company created by a team of SDSU CS514 students. 
                We're building a database-driven app that helps hungry people discover restaurants
                through a simple swipe, with a filtering system to ensure the best options available.
            </p>

            <h2>Our Mission</h2>
            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                To make every dining decision quick, confident, and stress-free by matching you to restaurants that fit your taste, budget and location. 
                To find what's right, you can rely on BiteSwipe!

            <h2>The Problem</h2>
            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                Finding a restaurant can be frustrating after scrolling through endless reviews and lists.
                There are many choices and factors to weigh in, like taste, budget and location.
                A simple decision can turn into a long search and when you're eating with others,
                finding the right place everyone likes is much harder.
            </p>

            <h2>Value to Users</h2>
            <p class="text-white max-w-2xl">
                With BiteSwipe, you spend less time searching and more time eating. 
                With our swipe-based approach, you can easily find restaurants that fit your preferences
                in terms of rating, price, distance and cuisine. Whether you are craving something familiar or
                trying something new, BiteSwipe helps you decide with confidence. 
            </p>

            <h2>Meet the Team</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 max-w-2xl w-full">
                {team.map((member) => (
                    <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/10 p-4 text-white">
                    <p class="font-bold">{member.name}</p>
                    <p class="text-sm">{member.role}</p>
                </div>
                ))}
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>